#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Deliberately almost a no-op. Neither the connection list nor the sudoers
# entries nor the systemd units are touched -- they belong to the system,
# not to this plugin.
set -uo pipefail

CONF="${OMARCHY_VPN_CONNECTIONS:-$HOME/.config/omarchy/vpn-connections.json}"
cat <<EOF2
Nothing to do. The connection list is kept:
  $CONF

Not removed, because they live outside this plugin:
  /usr/local/bin/omarchy-vpn-privileged
  /usr/local/bin/omarchy-vpn-import
  /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/org.omarchy.smartalbvpn.import.policy
  /etc/sudoers.d/smartalb-vpn
  /etc/openvpn/client/*.conf and /etc/wireguard/*.conf
Running connections keep running.

Configurations created through the widget likewise stay behind in /etc.
Whoever wants to be rid of them removes them through the widget itself
before uninstalling (with 'also delete the file' ticked).

Also not removed, but pointing nowhere afterwards: the entry
  { "id": "smartalb.vpn" }
under bar.layout.right in ~/.config/omarchy/shell.json. Remove it by hand,
otherwise the bar keeps trying to load a plugin that is no longer there.
EOF2
